{"skill":{"slug":"deepresearchwork","displayName":"Deep Research Work From Xian.LaoJ"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770284984284,"changelog":"Initial release of Deep Research skill, a comprehensive research framework.\n\n- Provides a structured workflow for in-depth, multi-source research and verification.\n- Includes detailed steps for planning, gathering, analyzing, and synthesizing information.\n- Integrates web, content, and memory tools for thorough research and source evaluation.\n- Offers guidance on source credibility, temporal relevance, and balancing perspectives.\n- Supplies templates and best practices for generating structured research reports.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":2169,"sha256":"6b00a7275e5254927c939651d64885bf3f02302f8fbe8a2d20c29a9452094b57","contentType":null},{"path":"research_template.md","size":2465,"sha256":"03ff0f55897bee3d4cbb281a6b296c56a18a13c562a8e28062ad7a5dc1eb227f","contentType":null},{"path":"research_workflow.js","size":9713,"sha256":"e782baddda1312a8037df4cdea766fa3bb8db161baee73074665e27a9d10929d","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6395,"sha256":"72f3e9801779d8ddd215d1dad362fdd098ee25bb951863d393cc11918f5af3c9","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2124,"sha256":"a081a2c2b62c4223f10ba1c10ecb09824eca604aa18b1927b1201c250013b254","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034460435,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0dd773eac57a89985512e094e5235a326a33077cc97bab737f5e8d5a7277741e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0dd773eac57a89985512e094e5235a326a33077cc97bab737f5e8d5a7277741e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\nSuspicious High-Entropy/Eval files: 1\n\nThe skill bundle defines a 'deep-research' framework. The `SKILL.md` and `README.md` provide detailed instructions for an AI agent to conduct research using OpenClaw tools like `web_search`, `web_fetch`, and `browser`. The `research_workflow.js` file implements this logic, explicitly stating its intention to use these tools. All described actions and code logic are consistent with the stated purpose of comprehensive research and lack any evidence of intentional harmful behavior such as data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection with a harmful objective. The use of network and file access tools is directly aligned with the skill's legitimate function.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161530052},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":55,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789034460435},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This research skill is not malicious, but it needs review because its included JavaScript workflow can generate mock sources and placeholder findings while the package presents itself as real verified research.","dimensions":[{"detail":"External browsing, local report writing, and consulting prior research memory are proportionate for a research workflow, but users should know these actions may expose research topics to tools, logs, or saved files.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No install script, dependency manifest, remote payload retrieval, tool wrapping, or automatic execution mechanism was found in the inspected artifact files.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill openly asks agents to use web search, web fetch, browser, memory search, and write/edit tools for research, which fits the stated purpose, but the scope is broad and should stay user-directed.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifacts mention memory lookup and persistent research records, and the JavaScript logs the full research topic, but there are no background workers, services, privilege escalation, credential access, or cross-session hooks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The markdown purpose is coherent for a deep-research skill, but research_workflow.js does not perform real search, fetching, or verification; it generates mock URLs, mock content, fixed findings, and a fixed confidence score.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing or using this as an automated research implementation. The markdown workflow is reasonable, but the shipped JavaScript should be treated as demo or scaffold code unless it is changed to perform real retrieval and provenance tracking. Avoid sensitive research topics if console logs or saved research files may be retained.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Verified in the artifact: the package claims comprehensive web research and validation, while the JavaScript workflow is a mock scaffold and also references phase fields that are not placed on the research plan.\n[SQP-2] expected: The README's web, browser, memory, and write/edit tool list is expected for deep research, but privacy and local file effects are only implicitly disclosed.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Verified in research_workflow.js: helper methods return mock sources, mock content, fixed findings, and a fixed confidence value, which can mislead if treated as production research.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Verified in research_workflow.js: comments say real implementations would call web_search and web_fetch, but this file simulates those steps locally.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The JavaScript logs the raw research topic; this is a limited privacy issue rather than evidence of exfiltration or malicious behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034460435}}}}}